{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-09-19T17:56:27.867Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6-astra","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"c7f8ae6e4be7d5ffb5d45dea","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6-astra","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"medium","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gvnj","claim:pm-ul5lph","lineage:pm-gvnj","lineage:pm-vlnc","lineage:pm-92if","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gvnj+pm-ul5lph","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gvnj","claim:pm-ul5lph","lineage:pm-gvnj","lineage:pm-vlnc","lineage:pm-92if","lineage:pm-doxj"]}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## Review findings\nPR 1279 identified three related issues at the new SDK domain boundaries: Bash completion interpolated static values into shell source, score normalization spread all matched scores into Math.min/Math.max, and the completed search item retained historical CLI-only scope metadata.\n\n## Correctness and security boundaries\nBash compgen performs word expansion after source parsing, so one layer of double-quote escaping is insufficient. Static word lists must protect both stages. Dynamic helper output must also encode each word before compgen sees it. Tests run the generated completion function in a real Bash subprocess and assert that command substitutions and backticks do not execute, variables remain literal, and quotes/backslashes survive across six input routes.\n\nScore normalization scans extrema without variadic calls or a temporary values array. Two-argument Math.min/Math.max preserve existing non-finite semantics. The regression exercises 200000 distinct scores and verifies the range endpoints and an interior normalized value.\n\n## Verification and lineage\nBoth regressions failed against the prior implementation before code changes. Existing completion/search-cache suites and four TypeScript projects pass. Temporary-project lifecycle acceptance covers package activation, search, annotations, all shell renderers and immutable history. The parent decomposition remains complete; this child records defects found during its pre-merge review. Original historical metadata remains available in append-only history."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-19T17:56:27.867Z"}],"before_hash":"2102752e5d38458c96136c861e35f78ee7577a8ee228c54b7ddd6b32c7ab2cf4","after_hash":"1b37c06be4328fe06362282052f1c7585e7f3e648ab8ecba2f7cbf722335ed22","item_hash_version":3,"message":"Document review repro, expansion boundaries and regression design","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"114dd938121ff5f78fa42031296d15742c32266886218d6cf22d24816d6e430b"}
